 "description": "A continuation scored the way the verdict is (description; discarded seeds).\n\nPre-approved for one case: the curriculum's stage-3 verdict fails, the mutants pass, and the wild\ntype fails on the on-lawn onset rate alone. The fit minimises a distance, an RMS over 24\nstatistics, while the verdict is pass or fail on each, so a statistic a few tenths past its bar\nbarely moves the score (`onset_gap.json`: the fit's true on-lawn reversal starts are 3.0 a minute\nagainst real worms' 4.3, and its detected rate 1.5 against 2.3).\n\nFrom the stage-3 answer, sep-CMA on stage 3's objective (the six families plus tph-1's, pdfr-1's\nand tax-4's lawn differences, the mutants together half of it, the graded responsiveness guard and\nthe saturation guard) plus a hinge: 5 x the sum over statistics of max(0, |z| - bar)^2, the bar\n0.3 inside each pass rule (2.78 for a wild-type statistic, against 3.0781; 1.94 for a mutant's,\nagainst 2.24), z on the bands' scales at 200 animals as the grade reads them, compressed as the\nranking score compresses it (10\u00b7asinh(z/10)) so a statistic far off cannot swamp the rest. The\nsearch starts with stage 3's own per-parameter step sizes (its state saved at generation 132,\n`curriculum/state_stage3_gen132.pkl`: sigma 0.0224, steps 0.008-0.042), since the curriculum drops a\nstage's search state when the stage ends. A first launch with a uniform sigma0 of 0.03 was stopped\nafter 2 generations (`hinge_isotropic_aborted/`): it moved the sensitive parameters 3.5x further\nthan stage 3 had, pushing most candidates' statistics far past their bars (medians 417 and 709;\n`hinge_candidates.py`). 50\ngenerations, population 48 at 200 animals on 16 workers, readouts every 10 generations. The\nverdict, as stage 3's: the last answer graded with presence on 5 fresh populations passes the wild\ntype in at least 3 and tph-1 and tax-4 each in at least 3.\n\nSeeds: candidates 860,000,000 + 200\u00b7k + i, CMA 9500, readouts 861,000,000 + i, the grade\n862,000,000 + 200\u00b7g + i. Run from the repository root: `hinge.py [smoke]`.\n",
